      "text": "Notes on the autumn collection. The palette starts from a neutral color base: charcoal wool, linen and plain white cotton. Against it the studio layers deep reds, a burgundy velvet and a lavender silk that reads as violet under warm light.\n\nSeveral pieces use metallic thread. The gold metallic trim on the jackets catches the light without looking cheap, and a few scarves carry a chrome finish that the buyers called silver. Accessories stay quiet: black leather, a navy belt and a cobalt clasp that only shows when the coat is open.\n\nThe spring line will move toward a cool color story. The team is testing teal, mint green and a soft azure, with coral and magenta reserved for the evening range. The one primary color the director refuses to use is yellow, though she allows amber buttons and a single rose lining.\n\nSwatches arrive on Monday. Anything that fades to gray after washing goes back to the mill.",
