      "id": "geography-document",
      "ontology": "geography-test",
      "kind": "document",
      "text": "Travel log, part two. We left London on a grey morning and crossed to France, where a friend who grew up in a small town near the Alps drove us to see Mont Blanc. From there the plan was simple: Rome for the Colosseum, then a ferry to Spain and a flight across the ocean.\n\nThe second half of the trip covered the Americas. In Mexico City we met a teacher who had lived in Chicago and LA and who described the United States as a nation of long drives. She told us to skip New York and head south instead, so we went on to Brazil and Argentina, which together made South America feel larger than any map suggests.\n\nOn the way home we spent a night in Sydney, though nobody in the group would call that Oceania in conversation. Next year the plan is Asia: Beijing, the Great Wall of China and a few days in Mumbai, which my grandmother still calls Bombay. England can wait.",
