              "ner": null
            }
          ],
          "derivation": "medicopilot.owl declares :Penetrating_Abdominal_Wound rdfs:seeAlso \"abdominal_wound+penetrating_wound\". A '+' synonym is a span rule: the first part is the key and the rest is content, matched in either order within 4 tokens, after the exact stage. The exact stage first makes \"penetrating wound\" penetrating_wound and \"to the abdomen\" abdominal_wound (a synonym of :Abdominal_Wound); the two are adjacent, so the span rule replaces both with penetrating_abdominal_wound, type spans. Outside live mode a span match takes its ner from the view's NER map by canonical form, which has no entry for penetrating_abdominal_wound, so ner is null. The audit missed it because it listed literal synonyms and did not model '+' span rules.",
